  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/paleont/DiagnosticFramework">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Diagnostic framework</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The standpoint from which a claim is made — modern
        biomedical, medieval humoral. Two individuals carry the entire
        perspectival argument: the same specimen seen through two
        incommensurable lenses.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/paleont/confidenceInterval">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">confidence interval</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/CalibratedInterval"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The statistical confidence at which the bounds are stated:
        "1 sigma", "95% CI", or "archaeological" for an interval that carries
        no statistical claim at all.

        Decision D7. Without this, CQ4b compares two intervals as if their
        endpoints were hard boundaries — which is the very reduction this
        project argues against, committed by our own query. A calibrated
        radiocarbon interval is not a fact with edges: it is a hedged
        estimate, and the source says so ("the precision of the radiocarbon
        dates of medieval samples are often better than ±25 to 30 years for
        the 1 sigma statistical uncertainty").

        Consequence: a disagreement computed from bare bounds is a claim about
        the bounds, not about the individual. queries/cq04b_tolerant.rq applies
        the source's OWN stated precision and reports a different — and, as it
        turns out, more faithful — result.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/paleont/data/tp292_claim_date_armPosition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/DatingClaim"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Archaeological date of Tirup 292. No radiocarbon date exists for this cemetery, so this specimen carries no dating disagreement</rdfs:label>
    <po:aboutSpecimen rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/data/tp292"/>
    <po:declaredIn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/data/schwarz2013"/>
    <po:framesContent rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/ModernBiomedical"/>
    <po:groundedIn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/data/tp292_obs_armPosition"/>
    <po:hasResult rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/data/tp292_interval_armPosition"/>
    <po:hedge rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/paleont/Certain"/>
